This is because the UI binds to the either SPARK_PUBLIC_DNS or the local hostname:

{code}
val host = Option(System.getenv(&quot;SPARK_PUBLIC_DNS&quot;)).getOrElse(Utils.localHostName())
{code}

One solution would be to have the web UI listen on all interfaces but generate links using SPARK_PUBLIC_DNS.  Even if user applications (like my IPython notebook) launch without setting SPARK_PUBLIC_DNS, we can rely on the Spark master having it set, so the master web UI will still be able to generate correct links to the application UIs.  However, this assumes that both web UIs are running on the same machine.

